From uc41a3e50d5c239de at groups.google.com  Mon Sep 22 08:31:05 2014
From: uc41a3e50d5c239de at groups.google.com (hipho...@gmail.com)
Date: Mon, 22 Sep 2014 08:31:05 +0000
Subject: Sample data sets are missing for some examples
Message-ID: <0MCQfThFPik.u0jV4W71YNkJ@sparkr-dev.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/sparkr-dev/c/0MCQfThFPik/m/u0jV4W71YNkJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

There are some examples in SparkR. However, there are no sample data sets for examples like kmeans, logistic regression, etc. It is not convenient for uses to have a try. Is it possible to add data generator or sample data sets in the SparkR package?  I tried to reuse the data generators in hibench() for wordcount & kmeans, but the data generated needs conversion, but it's hard for me to deduce the data format required by the SparkR examples from the source code.

From uf4108b5f63668d70 at groups.google.com  Mon Sep 22 19:48:48 2014
From: uf4108b5f63668d70 at groups.google.com (Shivaram Venkataraman)
Date: Mon, 22 Sep 2014 19:48:48 +0000
Subject: Re: Sample data sets are missing for some examples
Message-ID: <0MCQfThFPik.ckjrbmF1ShcJ@sparkr-dev.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <0MCQfThFPik.u0jV4W71YNkJ@sparkr-dev.groups.google.com>
References: <0MCQfThFPik.u0jV4W71YNkJ@sparkr-dev.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/sparkr-dev/c/0MCQfThFPik/m/ckjrbmF1ShcJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The SparkR examples follow the same input format as the Spark examples. So the data files at

https://github.com/apache/spark/blob/master/data/mllib/kmeans_data.txt
https://github.com/apache/spark/blob/master/data/mllib/lr_data.txt

should work for KMeans, LR.

We could definitely add similar sample files / document this format in our examples. Feel free to open PRs for such fixes !

Thanks
Shivaram

